{
  "dom_id": "step-q130731",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Suppose $C$ is a $9\\times 9$ matrix and $det(C)=-93.$ The matrix $D$ is obtained from $C$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{9}:=-\\frac{5}{31}{R}_{9}.$ What is the value of $det(D)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The row operation applied to $C$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $-\\frac{5}{31}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-\\frac{5}{31}det(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{31}\\cdot (-93) \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
